# Supabase & PostgreSQL RLS Security Standards

## Security Mandates
- Every table MUST have `ALTER TABLE table_name ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;` enabled.
- Never write open policies (`USING (true)`). Always verify `auth.uid() = user_id` or user role memberships.
- Differentiate between authenticated server clients (`createServerClient` with cookies) and admin service role keys.
- Never expose the `SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` in frontend client code or public GitHub repositories.
- Use database transactions (`BEGIN...COMMIT`) for multi-table relational inserts to prevent orphaned records.
